{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"26f3cb136d0366e2592a5fd8be2e771a38eed2c883348bfeb2bdfead6fb199f2","digest":{"component_or_area":"criteria eval CLI command preflight and gate-aware dispatch","key_entities":["src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py","tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py","plan_review.registry.by_id","code_review.registry.effective_criteria","calibrate_criterion","project.foo"],"problem_keywords":["criteria eval CLI","code-review criterion","admission","preflight validation","gate resolution","ambiguity detection"],"propositions":["The criteria eval CLI preflight rejects project code-review ids as unknown because it only checks plan_review.registry.by_id and never reaches the gate-aware resolver.","The preflight must admit an id if it exists in exactly one of plan-review or code-review registry and dispatch it to the corresponding gate's calibrate path.","An id active in both registries must be rejected as ambiguous with a message naming both gates; an id in neither must retain the existing unknown error.","The criteria eval CLI help text must include a concrete project code-review example (project.foo) alongside the plan-review example."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787580465767176001,"uuid":"5339405b-8478-4e3e-98ba-1a575c9569e3"}